WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.250
I've said it before and I will say it again
for a document summarizing and investigation

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.550
that supposedly totally clears the president.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:15.950
No collusion, no obstruction, which hunt presidential
harassment, all that stuff.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.440
Trump's going crazy to prevent the release
of the document, which supposedly totally

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.650
exonerates him.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.940
And the big news that we learned from yesterday
is that Donald Trump is asserting now executive

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.510
privilege over the entire unredacted Mueller
report.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.630
Uh, understand the sort of process that this
has gone through.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:40.960
Trump's attorney general, William Barr released
a redacted version of the Mueller report a

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.840
couple of weeks ago, and even in its redacted
form, it was absolutely devastating to Trump.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.360
It's cited, quote, substantial evidence of
obstruction of justice.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.600
It found, uh, it could not exonerate Donald
Trump from obstruction of justice.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.770
It found that of the 14 different possible
instances of obstruction, all three legal

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:05.280
requirements were met in eight of those 14
possible obstructive acts.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.709
That's really, really bad.

00:01:06.709 --> 00:01:10.030
But this was only the redacted version of
the report.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.119
And Democrats have been working to get their
hands on the unredacted version of the report

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:19.880
because there was so much blacked out material
in that redacted version pages and pages.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:25.079
Some pages have almost nothing other than
like the number of a footnote visible and

00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:26.689
the source of the footnote.

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:28.469
Everything else completely blacked out.

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:33.569
So Democrats understandably are thinking if
the redacted version is this devastating to

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:38.939
Donald Trump and the people around him, we've
got to get our hands on an unredacted version.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:45.789
And uh, William Barr has been resisting that,
uh, he has been going out of his way to stonewall

00:01:45.789 --> 00:01:47.939
those requests at every opportunity.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:53.630
And now that it's starting to look a little
dicey for William Barr, Trump has asserted

00:01:53.630 --> 00:02:00.469
executive privilege over the entire report
in order to hide those redacted portions before

00:02:00.469 --> 00:02:01.799
go any further.

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:03.649
What is executive privilege?

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:08.850
Executive privilege is the privilege claimed
by the president for the executive branch

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.310
of the United States government.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.690
And that's key because it relates to coequal
branches of government.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:19.820
It's the privilege of withholding information
in the public interest.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:25.390
This is all coming to a head because House
Democrats are looking at holding Attorney

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:30.730
General William Barr in contempt of Congress
for his refusal to release to them.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.210
The unredacted version of the report.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:38.830
Trump jumping in now and asserting executive
privilege is an attempt to preempt this and

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:43.340
get around the entire conversation about contempt
of Congress by William Barr.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.820
And the crazy thing about this is that the
report has endless evidence of obstruction,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.510
which his attorney general Trump's attorney
general William Barr, is refusing to release,

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.510
which is another obstructive act.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:03:00.670
In other words, Barr is obstructing in order
to prevent more evidence of Trump's obstruction

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:06.040
to be public, which now Donald Trump is compounding
by asserting executive privilege, which is

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.500
in and of itself another obstructive act,
although unlikely to be one that rises to

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.430
the level of criminality.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.930
What does Sarah Huckabee Sanders say about
all of this?

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:21.070
She's saying that the people breaking the
law are the members of the house who are trying

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.530
to do oversight.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:28.510
Take a look at this quote where she said yesterday
the American people see through chairman Nadler's

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.120
desperate ploy to distract from the president's.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.180
Historically successful agenda that's a lie
and are booming economy.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:42.350
Neither the White House nor attorney general
Barr will comply with chairman Nadler's unlawful

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.070
and reckless demands.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.610
Nothing unlawful about them.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.850
Reckless is of course, subjective faced with
Chairman Nadler's blatant abuse of power.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:56.410
There is no such abuse and at the Attorney
General's request, the president has no other

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:01.270
option than to make a protective assertion
of executive privilege.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.569
Almost nothing that she said is true.

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:07.500
I think we could agree that she used exclusively
words from the English language.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.300
Beyond that, I don't think I would agree about
anything in that statement with Sarah Huckabee

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.069
Sanders, the president's agenda is not historically
successful.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:17.620
The demands from the house are not unlawful.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.599
They're proper legal requests.

00:04:19.599 --> 00:04:24.159
I don't even want to talk about the Mueller
report itself here because this is about a

00:04:24.159 --> 00:04:25.960
much bigger crisis.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:32.939
The administration has flouted what is supposed
to be balanced power and checks and balances

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:38.030
as established by the founders of the United
States of America.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:44.189
Republican indifference is allowing this to
continue coequal branches of government, right?

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:49.200
That requires that when Trump disregards the
framework of how those checks and balances

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.220
work, the House and Senate need to balance
it out and go beyond partisanship.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.060
But Republicans simply refuse.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:01.810
The attorney general says, Trump can legally
stop any investigation into himself.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.999
The Justice Department says, you can't or
you don't, or you shouldn't indict a sitting

00:05:06.999 --> 00:05:09.139
president of the United States.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:11.220
What matters is they won't do it.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.979
This is not presidential harassment.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:17.779
This is a de facto presidential immunity that
goes completely outside what the founders

00:05:17.779 --> 00:05:20.229
of the country actually wanted an intended.

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:24.740
If we care about what the founders wanted
and intended, which the constitutional conservative

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:28.940
right claims to you have to call this out
as sickening, you have to call Republican's

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.830
out for standing by and implicitly rubber
stamping it by their inaction.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:37.360
And it has to end in one way, shape, or form.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.000
Unfortunately, the most direct path to ending
it, it's probably going out and voting Trump

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.320
out in November of 2020 because there's no
evidence anyone in power on the Republican

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:51.659
side, uh, is going to actually take any decisive
action here.

00:05:51.659 --> 00:05:53.480
And that's maybe the biggest tragedy of it
all.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:56.139
That goes beyond the content of the Mueller
report.

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:00.280
It goes beyond Trump's 14 potentially obstructive
acts.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.150
It's more about what does this mean?

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:06.839
It's about the basic foundations our country
is built on and I see it going nowhere.

00:06:06.839 --> 00:06:07.839
Quite frankly.

00:06:07.839 --> 00:06:09.250
If you disagree with me, let me know.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.850
I'm on Twitter at d pacman.

